# Strangler-fig demo context

This repository is a **strangler-fig migration demo** (Cursor SDK orchestrator + osTicket), not a general osTicket contribution fork.

## Prefer these areas

- `orchestrator/` — pipeline stages, agents, SDK wrappers, Linear/Slack
- `include/Services/` — extracted service classes
- `legacy/harness/` and `orchestrator/fixtures/` — parity capture/compare
- Seam patches named by the current ticket's seam manifest (`facadeFile`, `extractionTarget`)

Do **not** treat the upstream osTicket README or contribution guidance as the source of truth for how to work in this repo.

## Parity gate is sacred

- Never skip, weaken, or bypass the verifier.
- Do not open a PR or move a Linear ticket to **In Review** if parity fails.
- On parity or publish/PR failure, move the ticket to **Blocked** (not In Progress) so the listener can pick up the next Ready ticket.
- Never invent expected values or edit fixtures just to make a run pass.

## Leave unrelated trees alone

Do not edit `include/*/vendor/`, mpdf/laminas vendor trees, or unrelated osTicket files unless the current ticket's seam manifest **explicitly** names them.

## Nested cloud agents (no Docker)

Cartographer and fixture-generator run in Cursor cloud VMs. They must **not** start
Docker, DinD, `docker compose`, or `scripts/local-demo-start.sh`. Parity Compose
runs only on the local demo machine (`listener.ts` / `assertLocalDockerReady`).
